Software derived from Laya
--------------------------

This product includes software derived from Laya:
https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya
Developed by Convai Innovations and Laya contributors. Licensed under Apache-2.0.
Source revision: 4066d5d.

The decision model's design and training recipe follow Laya's: an encoder with a
question-type embedding and transformer layers on top, one [MASK] marker per option
scored to one logit, soft targets, and per-type temperature calibration. The
following files are adapted from Laya's code and carry a notice at the top stating
what they were derived from and how they were changed:

  * dadvar/text.py, dadvar/sequence.py, dadvar/model.py and dadvar/batch.py, from
    laya/common.py (option rendering, sequence construction, DecisionModel,
    collate_items).
  * training/finetune.py and training/prepare_data.py, in part, from
    notebooks/laya_finetune_typed_decisions_2xT4_kaggle.ipynb (temperature fitting,
    optimizer setup, the training item format).
  * benchmarks/metrics.py, in part, from laya/common.py (ece_score) and the
    evaluation in the same notebook.
  * .github/workflows/ci.yml and .github/dependabot.yml, from Laya's.

The rest of the repository (data/, the benchmark runner and diagnostics, the
training data recipe, balancing and validation) is original to this project.


Data formats and question wording from third parties
----------------------------------------------------

  * The row schema (id, state, questions, gold) and the gold answer format
    follow the LocalLLaMA/typed-decisions dataset, Apache-2.0:
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/LocalLLaMA/typed-decisions
  * The HelpSteer attribute definitions quoted in
    data/templates/helpsteer/_attributes.yaml are from NVIDIA's dataset cards,
    CC-BY-4.0: https://huggingface.co/datasets/nvidia/HelpSteer2
    The per-level wording is this project's.
  * The STS-B level wording follows the SemEval STS annotation guidelines
    (Agirre et al.); see data/templates/stsb/default.yaml.
  * The request and answer shapes are TypeSafe's System One API, used through
    the typesafe-sdk package (MIT), which is a dependency and is not included
    here: https://github.com/typesafe-ai/typesafe-sdk-python


